&lt;p&gt;Moloco is a truly rewarding place to work and in an exciting period of growth, which you could be a part of. Join us today and apply now!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You’ll Be Contributing to Moloco&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Design and deliver cutting-edge machine learning models that power Moloco’s Commerce Media products, serving as the core “engine” behind ads ranking, recommendations and search for retail media customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advance the performance, scalability, and reliability of our core ad prediction and retrieval systems so customers can unlock meaningful business outcomes from their first campaigns onward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and productionize core ML models for CTR prediction, retrieval, conversion, and search/recommendation that directly drive performance for Moloco Commerce Media customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end experimentation cycles, from problem framing and offline modeling to online A/B testing and iteration, to continuously improve auction, ranking, and recommendation quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, engineering, and solutions teams to translate retail media and ecommerce requirements into robust ML solutions, features, and evaluation frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical excellence across the ML stack by improving pipelines, model serving, and monitoring for low-latency, high-throughput, and highly reliable inference at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and uplevel other machine learning engineers through design reviews, knowledge sharing, and best practices in modern ML and MLOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Do I Know if the Role is Right For Me?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring 8-12 years of experience in applied machine learning or machine learning engineering, with a track record of shipping production models in ads, recommender systems, search, or large-scale ecommerce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply deep hands-on expertise with modern ML toolchains (e.g., Python, PyTorch/TensorFlow/JAX, feature stores, distributed training, and large-scale data processing frameworks) to solve complex ranking and prediction problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate experience building and optimizing models such as CTR predictors, retrieval models, conversion models, or recommendation systems, ideally including exposure to transformer-based architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguity by breaking loosely defined or novel business problems into well-structured ML projects, defining metrics, setting up experiments, and iterating based on data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively with cross-functional partners, tailoring complex technical concepts for non-technical stakeholders to drive alignment and decision-making across product, engineering, and go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead as the most senior technical IC on a team, independently owning high-impact technical initiatives, influencing architecture and roadmap decisions, and setting a high bar for code quality and model performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a fast-moving environment where combining rigorous experimentation with pragmatic engineering unlocks measurable value for advertisers, retailers, and end customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
